import{_ as t,o,c as i,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.UjrY2eRK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Use openid-client for Operator authentication","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"architecture/adr/0025-use-openid-client-for-operator-authentication.md","filePath":"architecture/adr/0025-use-openid-client-for-operator-authentication.md","lastUpdated":1788169631000}'),a={name:"architecture/adr/0025-use-openid-client-for-operator-authentication.md"};function r(s,e,d,c,l,p){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="use-openid-client-for-operator-authentication" tabindex="-1">Use openid-client for Operator authentication <a class="header-anchor" href="#use-openid-client-for-operator-authentication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Use openid-client for Operator authentication&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The Bun-only operator surface will use exactly pinned <code>openid-client</code> 6.8.7 for OIDC discovery, confidential Authorization Code plus PKCE, verified ID-token claims, and end-session URL construction. Gateway-owned modules retain the fixed routes, one-use five-minute login attempts, <code>(issuer, subject)</code> Operator Identity projection, group policy, and opaque Operator Sessions; <code>oidc-provider</code> 9.11.3 is test-only and runs in a Node child for deterministic Pocket-ID-like and Authentik-like contract profiles.</p><p>That deterministic suite is the fast protocol gate. Container CI additionally exercises the assembled production image against pinned disposable Pocket ID and Authentik services, including allowed and denied users, exact redirect and logout URIs, session creation, deep-link preservation, provider-outage isolation, and browser proof. Pull requests run the deterministic gate and Pocket ID compatibility; scheduled and release-capable runs also require Authentik compatibility.</p><p>Better Auth 1.7.2 is rejected because its built-in model conflicts with mandatory behavior: it gives OAuth state a ten-minute lifetime and consumes it non-atomically, requires email-centered users and fallback linking, persists provider tokens, exposes a broader route model, lacks independent idle/absolute expiry and both session caps, and cannot atomically create the identity and session through Bun SQLite. Its measured feature-import proxy was also materially larger than the selected protocol module. The complete evidence is recorded in <a href="./../../research/issue-22-oidc-session-selection.html">the issue 22 research note</a>.</p><p>This decision supersedes only ADR 0023&#39;s three-package workspace runtime ceiling by adding <code>openid-client</code> as a fourth, Bun-only dependency. The Worker continues to contain only its pre-existing Drizzle, <code>jose</code>, and Zod graph, enforced by a normalized source-map guard.</p><p>No provider token or raw claim is retained. Local Operator Session revocation is therefore the only guaranteed logout behavior; a discovered provider logout without an ID-token hint is best effort and cannot promise a portable post-logout return for both Pocket ID and Authentik. The production administration database, routes, cookies, and isolation composition remain owned by the separate Bun administration-foundation decision and implementation.</p>',6)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
